findings.description:
Line 93 says "Euler integration is simplest ... Verlet or semi-implicit Euler may be needed", which leaves the choice open. Slice 100 (`100-slices.behavior-engine.md` line 17) already commits to semi-implicit Euler. Verlet would need a previous-position array that line 39 does not include.

The document also omits what the flocking model needs to stay stable:
- a maximum speed clamp and a maximum force clamp;
- normalization of alignment and heading vectors, which is undefined for zero velocity;
- weight normalization so profile weights are comparable across forces;
- the timestep, its value, and its relation to the 20–60 Hz tick rate (300-arch line 78).

Without a speed limit, boid systems commonly diverge or stall. Record the integrator, the clamp policy, and `dt` in the document, as engine constants or as explicit profile fields.
